            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) fit was assessed using RMSE, MAE, MSE, and R\u00b2. The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) performance was evaluated using standard metrics, including Root Mean Square Error (RMSE). The model evaluation metrics (Table 3) indicate a strong predictive performance of the LMM in estimating groundwater levels. The RMSE value of 1.31 suggests that, on average, the predicted groundwater levels deviate from the observed values by approximately 1.31 m. This level of error is considered low and acceptable, particularly in hydrological modeling where natural variability is high. Among the four districts (Table 4), Khorda exhibits the best model performance, with the lowest RMSE (0.70)... Patna also demonstrates strong model performance, with an RMSE of 0.77... Ranchi has slightly higher error values (RMSE=1.16...)... In contrast, Kolkata records the highest error metrics (RMSE=2.11...)",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
