            "target_entity_instance": "MAE",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) fit was assessed using RMSE, MAE, MSE, and R\u00b2. The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) performance was evaluated using standard metrics, including Mean Absolute Error (MAE). The MAE of 0.92 further supports the model's precision, indicating that the average absolute difference between the observed and predicted values is less than one meter. This reinforces the reliability of the predictions without being disproportionately affected by outliers, as MAE is a robust metric for overall accuracy. Among the four districts (Table 4), Khorda exhibits the best model performance, with the lowest MAE (0.61)... Patna also demonstrates strong model performance, with an MAE of 0.62... Ranchi has slightly higher error values (MAE=0.86)... In contrast, Kolkata records the highest error metrics (MAE=1.57...)",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
