            "target_entity_instance": "MSE",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) fit was assessed using RMSE, MAE, MSE, and R\u00b2. The Linear mixed-effects model (LMM) performance was evaluated using standard metrics, including Mean Squared Error (MSE). The Mean Squared Error (MSE) of 1.72 aligns with the RMSE and confirms that the model errors are generally small and not heavily skewed by extreme deviations. A low MSE value indicates a good fit and a high degree of consistency between the model and the observed data. Among the four districts (Table 4), Khorda exhibits the best model performance, with the lowest MSE (0.48)... Patna also demonstrates strong model performance, with an MSE of 0.59... Ranchi has slightly higher error values (MSE=1.35)... In contrast, Kolkata records the highest error metrics (MSE=4.45...)",
